From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ori Pekelman <ori@pekelman.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 08:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ggml-cuda buffer_from_ptr: skip init_tensor row-padding memset

The BYO read-only mmap has no per-tensor padding bytes, so the standard
init_tensor's cudaMemset(data+original_size, 0, padded-original) writes
past the tensor into the read-only mapping -> illegal memory access for
any quantized tensor with ne0 % MATRIX_ROW_PADDING(512) != 0 (DeepSeek /
qwen3moe down_exps, ne0 = expert_ff = 1408/768; OLMoE's 1024 is exempt).
The zeroing is only a NaN-safety belt: matmul kernels zero-pad the input
vector, so weight_padding * 0 = 0 regardless. Override init_tensor=NULL
on the from_ptr buffer (already done for free_buffer). Unblocks every
quantized MoE model on CUDA (DeepSeek-V2 MLA, Qwen3-MoE, Qwen2-MoE).
---
--- a/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu	2026-06-29 08:08:12.351368534 +0000
+++ b/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu	2026-06-29 08:08:12.303346904 +0000
@@ -1078,6 +1078,16 @@
     // device buffer.
     if (buf) {
         buf->iface.free_buffer = ggml_backend_cuda_buffer_from_ptr_free;
+        // Skip the standard init_tensor's row-padding cudaMemset. For a
+        // BYO read-only mmap, the file has no per-tensor padding bytes, so
+        // the memset writes past the tensor's data into the read-only
+        // mapping (or the next tensor) → illegal memory access for any
+        // quantized tensor with ne0 % MATRIX_ROW_PADDING != 0 (e.g.
+        // DeepSeek/qwen3moe down_exps, ne0 = expert_ff = 1408/768). The
+        // zeroing is only a NaN-safety belt: matmul kernels zero-pad the
+        // INPUT vector, so weight_padding * 0 = 0 regardless of the
+        // padding bytes' contents. Caller owns the bytes.
+        buf->iface.init_tensor = NULL;
     }
     return buf;
 }
